This is a right-facing loose-ball pickup. There is no ball in the art: the game basketball is separately rendered. Both hands remain visibly empty; at floor contact, fingers touch only the empty floor plane with nothing between them. No basketball, sphere, seams, court, hoop, floor texture, shadow, background, glow, border, grid, text, teammate or opponent. Use true alpha-zero transparent exterior and gutters with no checkerboard, matte, haze or speckles.

Five distinct sequential poses:
0 Leo spots a loose ball to image-right, pivots and lowers his center of gravity;
1 takes a low forward step, right arm reaches toward the floor, left arm balances behind;
2 deepens the lunge, knees flex, empty right hand lowers to just above the ground;
3 GRAB at simulation tick7: right fingertips touch the empty ground plane at image-right, left arm counterbalances, torso stable;
4 rises into a composed ready stance, both hands empty and relaxed after securing the separate ball.

Leo remains right-facing. Keep complete adult human anatomy, pale skin, long waves, refined mustache, black/crimson kit and shoes consistent. Return only the transparent sprite sheet.
